 Working of Heap Sort
5.Build a Max Heap or Min Heap from the input array.
6.Swap the root element with the last element in the unsorted portion of the array.
7.Reduce the heap size so that the element placed at the end is no longer included in the heap.
8.Apply heapify to restore the heap property.
9.Repeat the process until all elements are in sorted order.
Algorithm: Ascending Order Using Max Heap
10.Start.
11.Read the product prices into an array.
12.Build a Max Heap from the array.
13.Swap the root (maximum value) with the last element of the heap.
14.Reduce the heap size by one and apply heapify.
15.Repeat the extraction and heapify steps until only one element remains.
16.Display the prices in ascending order.
17.Stop.
Algorithm: Descending Order Using Min Heap
18.Start.
19.Read the product prices into an array.
20.Build a Min Heap from the array.
21.Swap the root (minimum value) with the last element of the heap.
22.Reduce the heap size by one and apply heapify.
23.Repeat the extraction and heapify steps until only one element remains.
24.Display the prices in descending order.
25.Stop.
 Example
Consider the product prices: 50, 20, 40, 10, 30.
 Ascending Order Using Max Heap
Step 1: Initial array: [50, 20, 40, 10, 30]
Step 2: Build a Max Heap. One valid Max Heap representation is [50, 30, 40, 10, 20]. The root contains the maximum value, 50.
Step 3: Swap the root with the last element, reduce the heap size, and heapify the remaining elements. Repeat until the array is sorted.
Stage	Array / Result
Initial Max Heap	50, 30, 40, 10, 20
After first extraction and heapify	40, 30, 20, 10, 50
After second extraction and heapify	30, 10, 20, 40, 50
After third extraction and heapify	20, 10, 30, 40, 50
Final sorted array	10, 20, 30, 40, 50
Result: The prices are arranged in ascending order: 10, 20, 30, 40, 50.
Descending Order Using Min Heap
Using the same input array [50, 20, 40, 10, 30], build a Min Heap and repeatedly move the minimum value to the end of the unsorted portion, restoring the Min Heap property after each extraction.
Final sorted array in descending order: 50, 40, 30, 20, 10.
 Complexity Analysis
Operation / Case	Complexity
Best-case time complexity	O(n log n)
Average-case time complexity	O(n log n)
Worst-case time complexity	O(n log n)
Building the heap	O(n)
Auxiliary space for recursive heapify	O(log n)
Note: Heap Sort is an in-place sorting algorithm and uses O(1) auxiliary array storage. A recursive heapify implementation may use O(log n) call-stack space.
