Conclusion
Heap Sort is an efficient comparison-based sorting algorithm that uses a binary heap to arrange product prices. A Max Heap is used to sort prices in ascending order, while a Min Heap can be used to sort prices in descending order. It is useful for organizing online shopping product prices for analysis and reporting.
